From fa8c80ceccc5e28d93264962c56073375657919f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:05:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] video: rockchip: mpp: reject re-init of an already-bound
 session

MPP_CMD_INIT_CLIENT_TYPE binds a /dev/mpp_service session to a device: it
sets session->dma via mpp_dma_session_create(), session->mpp, the dev-ops
callbacks, and calls mpp_session_attach_workqueue(), which does an
unconditional list_add_tail() of session->session_link onto
queue->session_attach.

The handler has no guard against being called twice on the same session.
session->session_link is INIT_LIST_HEAD'd once at session creation, so a
first INIT_CLIENT_TYPE attaches cleanly but a second re-adds the
already-linked node, corrupting queue->session_attach. With
CONFIG_DEBUG_LIST this is a "list_add double add" WARN reached from
mpp_process_request(); on a production kernel the corruption is silent and
the taskqueue worker later walks a broken list. The second call also
overwrites session->dma without destroying the first, leaking the prior
DMA session.

Both are reachable from an unprivileged /dev/mpp_service fd (video group):
open, then issue INIT_CLIENT_TYPE twice. A legitimate client binds once, so
normal decode/encode is unaffected.

Reject a second bind with -EBUSY before mutating session state, closing
both the double-add and the dma-session leak. The unguarded sequence is
present in the pristine Rockchip 6.1 BSP (develop-6.1) too, where
mpp_common.c is byte-identical, so this is a latent BSP defect rather than
a forward-port regression.

Signed-off-by: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
index 8690232fd23eb..804e19e2eb969 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
@@ -1423,6 +1423,18 @@ static int mpp_process_request(struct mpp_session *session,
 		if (!mpp)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * INIT_CLIENT_TYPE binds the session to a device exactly once.
+		 * A second call would re-create session->dma (leaking the
+		 * first) and re-run mpp_session_attach_workqueue(), which
+		 * list_add_tail()s the already-linked session->session_link and
+		 * corrupts queue->session_attach (a DEBUG_LIST "list_add double
+		 * add", reachable from an unprivileged /dev/mpp_service fd).
+		 * Reject re-init.
+		 */
+		if (session->mpp)
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		session->device_type = (enum MPP_DEVICE_TYPE)client_type;
 		session->dma = mpp_dma_session_create(mpp->dev, mpp->session_max_buffers);
 		session->mpp = mpp;
